#metadata(title = "Mote Reference Parity", author = "Mote")

#document(
  page = { size = "letter" },
  margin = { top = pt(54), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(54), left = pt(72) }
)

#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { size = pt(10), color = "#111827" },
  paragraph = {
    spacing = {
      after = pt(7),
      line = { rule = "multiple", value = 1.08 }
    }
  }
)

#set paragraph(style = "Normal")

# Reference Parity

This case checks that DOCX, PDF, and PNG resolve the same label metadata even when the references appear before their targets.

Forward title: #ref(target = "later-heading", display = "title").

Forward page: #ref(target = "later-heading", display = "page", fallback = "2").

Forward figure number: #ref(target = "comparison-table", display = "number").

Styled internal link: [**jump to the later heading**](#later-heading).

#label("manual-anchor", title = "Manual target", number = "Exhibit 7")
#paragraph[Explicit metadata target.]

Explicit title: #ref(target = "manual-anchor", display = "title"). Explicit number: #ref(target = "manual-anchor", display = "number").

#break(type = "page")

#label("later-heading")
## Later Heading

The forward title above must read “Later Heading,” and its page reference must read “2.” In PDF the title and styled Markdown text are clickable internal links; PNG preserves the same visible text.

#figure(
  kind = "table",
  numbering = { enabled = true, id = "reference-tables", label = "Table" }
)[
  #label("comparison-table")
  #table(
    width = inch(5.75),
    layout = "fixed",
    alignment = "center",
    cell = {
      margin = { all = pt(6) },
      borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#64748b" } }
    }
  )[
    #row[
      #cell(width = inch(2.0), fill = "#dbeafe")[Target]
      #cell(width = inch(3.75), fill = "#eff6ff")[Expected visible reference]
    ]
    #row[
      #cell[Heading]
      #cell[Later Heading; page 2]
    ]
    #row[
      #cell[Figure]
      #cell[Table 1]
    ]
  ]
  #caption[Reference comparison]
]

Back references: #ref(target = "later-heading", display = "title"), #ref(target = "comparison-table", display = "title"), and #ref(target = "comparison-table", display = "number").

PASS: every backend shows the same titles, explicit number, page number, and generated table number without fallback placeholders.
